  <title>Orca Find</title>
  <p>
    Orca Find searches visible contents in the active window. When there is a match, Orca
    activates flat review and moves the review location to the matching item or text.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Find dialog lets you enter text to search for, choose whether to start from the current
    location or the top of the window, match case, match whole words, search backward, and wrap
    around. After you perform a search, use the Find commands to move to the next or previous
    match without reopening the dialog.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you have not searched yet, Find Next and Find Previous open the dialog. Search text is
    interpreted as a regular expression; characters such as a period or an asterisk have special
    meanings. Use a backslash before a special character to match it literally.
  </p>
  <p>
    Finding a match does not move application focus or reposition the caret.
  </p>
